From 96416ec463e31b538ce5ea4212fcd58c690d18a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:06:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/45] decide: full-path scoring

Full-path branch phase (spec 4): one sequence per option from
full_path_plan, rows tagged per trie node, decode chunks flushed at
n_batch tokens or llama_n_seq_max rows (a chunk may split a sequence),
full-vocabulary rows turned into node_logp (children, END on leaves,
MERGED per leaf child) and scored by score_field_full. Vocab index
built once per engine. Budget and seqs per state use the full-path
counts; usage counts tokens decoded and rows read; engine.scoring,
engine.resplit_options, coverage per field; info lists both modes;
dump entries carry mode, and full-path entries option, rows, logp.
The full_path guard in decide-api is removed.

Model-free tests: test-decide-fullpath (chunks, row mapping across a
split, row values, budget counts); leaf MERGED sets in test-decide-trie.
